Move the codec credits below the black hole where they are readable

The MozJPEG / libwebp / libavif / OxiPNG line sat a fixed gap under the drop
ring, which put it inside the accretion disk's glow at most viewport sizes --
low-contrast text on the brightest part of the render. It is now pinned to the
bottom edge, clear of the disk, with a shadow for the cases where a lensing arc
still reaches that far.

Taking it out of the centred flex column also fixes the ring's alignment. The
column was centred in the space below the header, so the ring sat half a header
height lower than the shadow it is meant to trace. The hero is now positioned
against the viewport instead, and pointer events are handed back to the button
alone so the layer does not swallow clicks elsewhere.

Tightened tracking and size below the sm breakpoint, where the four names at
full letter-spacing ran the entire width of a 375px screen.

